user: There's a charge on my account I don't recognize and I want to dispute it. Short answers are fine: how long do I have to file, and who actually decides it?
assistant: I’ll look up Cartwheel’s dispute/charge policy so I can give you the correct filing window and decision-maker.
tool_call: {"query": "charge dispute filing window who decides dispute"}
tool_result: {"ok": true, "results": [{"policy_id": "cw-disputes", "score": 11.205, "snippet": "# Cartwheel dispute policy\n\nBuyers can dispute a charge for up to 60 days after delivery. Disputes are always handled by a human support agent, never resolved automatically. Opening a dispute pauses any pending refund on the same order.", "title": "Cartwheel dispute policy"}, {"policy_id": "cw-getting-help", "score": 2.358, "snippet": "# Getting help on Cartwheel\n\nThe Cartwheel support assistant answers questions about orders, returns, refunds, products, and platform policy, and it cites the policy page behind every policy answer. If the assistant cannot resolve a case it opens a ticket for a human agent, who responds within 24 ho", "title": "Getting help on Cartwheel"}, {"policy_id": "cw-restocking-fees", "score": 1.732, "snippet": "# Cartwheel restocking fee policy\n\nA store may charge a restocking fee of up to 15 percent on returned items that have been opened. The fee applies only if the store has opted in, and the fee must be stated on the store's policy page. Unopened items are never charged a restocking fee.", "title": "Cartwheel restocking fee policy"}]}
assistant: You have **up to 60 days after delivery** to dispute a charge.

Disputes are decided by a **human Cartwheel support agent**, not automatically. Policy: **cw-disputes**.

